WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.620
I'm Mary Helen Bowers,

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.870
founder of Ballet Beautiful Fitness.

00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:31.700
I danced with New York
City Ballet for 10 years.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.280
Ballet Beautiful is really born

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.260
from my experience as
a professional dancer

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.010
and that whole life
experience of being a dancer,

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.590
which is so incredibly physical,

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.220
where you are using your
body to express your art.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.640
And I had to learn,

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.950
and it took a lot of trial and error

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.560
for me to figure out the best system

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.790
to take care of my body,

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.770
to prevent injury, to feel my strongest,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.420
my leanest, and my best.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.270
Once I left the company, I
took a break from dancing.

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:01.080
I needed time where I
wasn't in a dance studio,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.670
where I didn't have that pressure

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.690
to look a certain way,
to perform a certain way.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.560
And when I wanted to start working out

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.630
I had gained weight, my body had changed.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.030
I also didn't want to go
back into a ballet studio,

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.300
I felt self-conscious.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.480
So I started picking up
with my old exercises.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:19.470
I would do 45 minutes a day.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.460
And my body started to change.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.600
I got leaner and really
all of my ballet muscles

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.380
kind of came back into use.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.060
And with that process, my
whole body began to change.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.230
I started sharing my workout with friends.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:36.280
All of our clients have really been built

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.910
through word of mouth.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.340
One of the first Victoria's Secret Angels

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.640
that I worked with was Miranda Kerr,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.360
who is a long-time client and a very

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.400
dear friend of mine.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.840
We're still working together today.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.700
And it's been fun to train
with people like Miranda

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.040
and like Lily Aldridge.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.120
Through having a baby,

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.030
through, maybe, a second pregnancy.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.510
For some people it's
through multiple seasons

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.670
of doing a show like Victoria's Secret,

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.960
or a big film, or runway moment.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.750
But it's been really
exciting, too, for me,

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:13.733
to take these women through
some really momentous

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.570
moments in their careers.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.920
And be there to support them,

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.730
to help them feel strong,
to help them feel confident,

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.805
and perform at their best level as well.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.980
With the Angels, they're
training really, really, hard.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.350
I'm using ballet inside the workout,

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:36.124
but I'm thinking of it as
a really, really focused,

00:02:36.124 --> 00:02:38.260
crazy, I want the deepest burn.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.210
I want to give them the biggest impact.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:44.550
We're trying to make their
abs as toned as possible,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.800
to make their butts as
lifted and toned as possible,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.700
to give them sleek definition
through their legs.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.070
And beautiful posture
and strength to hold,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.170
those wings for example,
which really weigh a lot.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.730
So it's not that I'm giving them a workout

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.400
that someone else couldn't do.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.670
But certainly we are doing a really

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.613
intensified version of the program.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.238
A mutual friend that I had danced with,

00:03:11.238 --> 00:03:14.130
with New York City Ballet,
connected me with Natalie.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.410
She was in town.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.600
She was looking for a new trainer

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.150
and for somebody to help
prepare her for "Black Swan."

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.760
She danced really seriously until

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.300
she was about 12 or 13, when
her acting career took off.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.650
So we had to kind of bring her up to speed

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.123
with her dancing.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.390
"Black Swan," I think, played a huge role

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.810
in bringing ballet into the spotlight,

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:42.290
making it cool, making it hip
and relevant in pop culture.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:45.850
And of course, Natalie's
role in that was huge.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:49.160
And I was so fortunate to have been

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.738
such a big part of that film.

00:03:51.738 --> 00:03:55.085
And it also brought ballet fitness

00:03:55.085 --> 00:03:59.749
into the press, into I
think, the sort of lexicon

00:03:59.749 --> 00:04:02.183
of the everyday woman.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.210
You don't have to be a professional dancer

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.780
or to have trained your
body for a dozen years

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.470
to experience ballet, to
bring it into your home.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.870
You feel better, you have more energy.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:16.290
Your body feels stronger.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.470
You start to see results.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.909
It's really, really motivating.

00:04:19.909 --> 00:04:23.508
And as you get going, you
can build that momentum

00:04:23.508 --> 00:04:26.750
to make fitness a more
regular part of your life,

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.160
a larger part of your life.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.670
You can prioritize.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.957
And it takes some work to say,

00:04:31.957 --> 00:04:35.350
"I'm gonna carve this
time out just for me."

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.970
Don't wait for life to be perfect

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:40.990
because it's busy and it's messy,

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.273
and you just have to start where you are.

